## Your rights

You have the right to access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18) and data portability (Art. 20). Write to {{ controller.privacy_contact }} with a link or a short description of the text that concerns you. We answer within one month.

## Your right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)

**You can object at any time, for reasons arising from your particular situation, to the processing of personal data about you that is based on our legitimate interest.** Write to {{ controller.privacy_contact }}. We then stop processing the text in question, delete it from our collections and add it to a suppression list, so that it is not collected again and not used for future training, unless we can show compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests.

Please do not post personal details in public GitHub issues. The issue template "Rights request" is only for requests that contain no personal data, such as opt-outs of whole websites.

